    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;be non-zero real numbers that are, respectively, the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>th</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>100</mn><mrow><mi>th</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1000</mn><mrow><mi>th</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;terms of a harmonic progression. Consider the system of linear equations<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1000</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>List-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>, then the system of linear equations has</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;as a solution</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>II</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>100</mn></math>, then the system of linear equations has</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;as a solution</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>III</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>10</mn></math>, then the system of linear equations has</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>infinitely many solutions</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>IV</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>, then the system of linear equations has</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>no solution</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfenced></math></td>\t\t\t<td>at least one solution</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>The correct option is:</p>"
